// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's opening walk, measured 2026-08-08; the
// mechanism narration corrected same day): a closure performing E,
// ESCAPING its install, called outside — the shape capabilities forbid
// and the modal calculus re-admits under proof. Mentl ADMITS it: with
// one E-handler in the program the op dispatches by the STATIC
// SINGLETON tier (a direct call — the escaped call runs the handler's
// value); under multiple handlers the dynamic innermost install wins
// (mn-escape-innermost pins 20); with NO handler reaching the root the
// executable REFUSES (E_EffectUnhandled, armed — nothing executes
// unproven). No negation in scope here: expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(1) }
fn make() = () => op()
fn escaped() = (make()) ~> h
fn main() = escaped()()
